* {{enPR|rĕkʹərd|rĕkʹôrd|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛk.ɚd/|/ˈɹɛk.oɹd/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-record-noun.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhyme|en|ɛkɔː(ɹ)d|ɛkə(ɹ)d|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|rec|ord}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# An item of [[information]] put into a temporary or permanent physical [[medium]].
#: {{ux|en|The person had a '''record''' of the interview so she could review her notes.}}
#: {{ux|en|The tourist's photographs and the tape of the police call provide a '''record''' of the crime.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|year=2012
|month=March-April
|author=John T. Jost
|title=Social Justice: Is It in Our Nature (and Our Future)?
|volume=100
|issue=2
|page=162
|magazine=w:American Scientist
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/social-justice-is-it-in-our-nature-and-our-future
|passage=He draws eclectically on studies of baboons, descriptive anthropological accounts of hunter-gatherer societies and, in a few cases, the fossil '''record'''.
|accessdate=19 May 2013
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120213062813/http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/social-justice-is-it-in-our-nature-and-our-future
|archivedate=13 February 2012
}}
# Any instance of a physical medium on which information was put for the purpose of preserving it and making it available for future reference.
#: {{syn|en|log}}
#: {{ux|en|We have no '''record''' of you making this payment to us.}}
#: {{ux|en|My remarks were struck from the '''record'''.}}
# {{ellipsis of|en|phonograph record|t=a [[disc]], usually made from [[vinyl]], on which sound is recorded and may be replayed on a [[phonograph]]}}.
#: {{syn|en|disc|phonograph record|vinyl}}
#: {{ux|en|I still like '''records''' better than CDs.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Record Doctor|year=2012|artist={{w|Saint Etienne (band)|Saint Etienne}}|passage=He's the '''record''' doctor / Tell him your woes / He'll reach in his bag / And he'll give you a dose}}
## {{lb|en|by extension|informal}} A music [[album]]; broadly, any music released as a single, EP, etc.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A set of [[data]] relating to a single individual or item.
#: {{ux|en|Pull up the '''record''' on John Smith. What's his medical history?}}
# {{lb|en|data structure}} A [[data structure]] similar to a [[struct]], in some [[programming language]]s such as [[C#]] and [[Java]] based on [[class]]es and designed for storing [[immutable]] [[data]].
#: {{cot|en|struct|enumeration}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Elliot B. Koffman|title=Pascal: Problem Solving and Program Design|year=1989|publisher=Addison-Wesley|page=406|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dBUiAQAAIAAJ&q=%22record%22+pascal&dq=%22record%22+pascal&hl=&cd=3&source=gbs_api|isbn=978-0-201-11834-6|passage=This chapter examines another data structure, the '''record''' (available in Pascal but not in all other high-level languages). '''Records''' make it easier to organize and represent information in Pascal, a major reason for the popularity of the Pascal{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ian F. Darwin|title=Java Cookbook|year=2020|publisher=O'Reilly Media|page=232|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H9PXDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA232&dq=%22record%22+type+Java&hl=&cd=9&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22record%22%20type%20Java&f=false|isbn=978-1-4920-7255-3|passage=The new '''record''' type provides another solution. A '''record''' is a class-like construct for data classes, a restricted form of class like enums and annotations.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joseph Albahari|title=C# 9.0 in a Nutshell|year=2021|publisher=O'Reilly Media|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=uUwgEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA210&dq=%22record%22+C#&hl=&cd=15&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22record%22%20C#&f=false|isbn=978-1-0981-0093-3|page=210|passage=A '''record''' is a special kind of class that's designed to work well with immutable (readonly) data.}}
# The most extreme known value of some variable, particularly that of an [[achievement]] in competitive events.
#: {{ux|en|The heat and humidity were both new '''records'''.}}
#: {{ux|en| Australia set a '''record''' of 10 back-to-back T20I wins.}}
#: {{ux|en| He broke the '''record''' for the youngest English captain.}}
#: {{ux|en|The team set a new '''record''' for most points scored in a game.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 April 5|title=Network News: Conservatives accused of "rewarding Avanti's failure"|journal=RAIL|issue=980|page=6|text="Avanti has literally broken '''records''' over the last six months for delays and cancellations, and the Conservatives' answer is to reward failure with millions more in taxpayer cash," said Labour Shadow Transport Secretary Louise Haigh.}}

